---
import Layout from "../layouts/BlogPost.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="Who Are We"
	description="Origin story of TLC Labs"
	pubDate={new Date("Sept 8 2026")}

>
	<h2>Our Vision</h2>
	<p>
		<em
			>*"To fundamentally improve the lives of people by creating a compassionate, employee-first business model, while building reliable open-source appliances that help eliminate e-waste"</em
		> - TLC Labs
	</p>

	<h2>Core Identity: T.L.C.</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Trust</strong> - Trust is our foundation and our north star for
			building relationships with both employees and people.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Longevity</strong> - We are building an ever-lasting institution
			that produces devices and relationships designed to stand the test of
			time.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Community</strong> - We prioritize our people and foster a community
			where our employees are loved.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Operational Hierarchy</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>First - Our Employees:</strong> We believe that happy employees
			will naturally keep our people happy, which in turn creates a prosperous
			company.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Second - People:</strong> We are dedicated to providing unbelievable
			hospitality alongside high-quality products.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Third - Income &amp; Longevity:</strong> We must generate income
			to stay afloat, operating with a mindset of surviving for "5 more years,
			every year".
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What We Do &amp; How We Earn</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Product Focus:</strong> We develop competitive mid-range to high-range
			open-source appliances.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Manufacturing Method:</strong> Our devices are built using a combination
			of 3D-printed parts and standard off-the-shelf hardware and electronics.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Revenue Streams:</strong> We generate income strictly by selling
			pre-assembled devices, self-assembly kits, and standalone hardware components.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Business Structure:</strong> We operate as a registered Sole Proprietor
			in Saskatchewan but are built upon a Social Enterprise (B-Corp) model.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Structural Empathy (How We Work)</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>10:1 Pay Ratio:</strong> Company leaders and the CEO will never
			earn more than ten times the salary of our lowest-paid employee.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>32-Hour Work Week:</strong> We mandate a 4-day work week, so employees
			receive 40-hour pay for 32 hours of work, allowing them more time with
			their families.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Mandatory Rest:</strong> We provide competitive benefits, including
			6 weeks of vacation, 4 of which are mandatory to ensure a rested and sturdy
			mind.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Our Promise to People</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Vocabulary Shift:</strong> We do not use the word "Customers";
			we only serve, build for, and help "People".
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Absolute Ownership:</strong> We embrace true transparency, open-source
			principles, and the absolute right-to-repair, so people truly own what
			they buy.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>No Subscriptions:</strong> We refuse to drain the wallets of our
			people and guarantee absolutely no subscriptions.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Environmental Impact:</strong> We are committed to reducing e-waste
			and will explore circular-economy initiatives like plastic recycling discounts.
		</li>
	</ul>
</Layout>
